    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The legacy quick-service restaurant operations are showing clear operational momentum, with profitability rebounding meaningfully from prior losses and the company ending the year with a fortified cash position. However, the business’s entire industry exposure is set to change radically as the proposed merger with Aero Velocity advances; the transaction will pivot the company away from restaurants and into aerospace and AI, leaving the ultimate role—or retention—of the legacy food-service segment uncertain.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has successfully engineered an operational turnaround, sharply narrowing losses and restoring credibility with improved restaurant-level performance. At the same time, management is aggressively redirecting corporate strategy through the transformative Aero Velocity merger, effectively using the existing public-company shell to enter high-tech sectors. The market’s enthusiastic reaction suggests confidence in their ability to execute both the restaurant restructuring and the complex pivot, though the radical nature of the shift introduces significant integration and execution risk.",
